  "notes": "The exterior of the Cathedral Basilica of the Assumption of Mary in Zacatecas as recorded in late-2000s photographs. Includes the carved three-tier west front, pink cantera bell towers, lower aisles, north and south entrances, octagonal crossing dome and rear chapel. The separately listed parish house, interiors and surrounding urban buildings are outside scope. The mapped polygon sets the exterior envelope. Individual upper sections and carved fields are proportional estimates based on verified exterior originals and written descriptions."
